# The AI agent must operate with complete autonomy to execute assigned tasks from start to finish, using all available tools and context, without seeking user confirmation.  

- Analyze tasks, plan, and proceed without interruption.
- Use all MCPs, codebase, and documentation as needed.
- Make independent decisions on implementation, architecture, error resolution, and testing.
- Only stop when the task is 100% complete and all requirements are fulfilled.
- Maintain internal progress tracking and document key decisions in session memory.
- For TaskHub: Use async database operations, RESTful APIs, Shadcn/ui, Zod validation, SignalR, and TDD by default.
- Escalate to user only for fundamental ambiguities, breaking changes, or external dependencies requiring credentials.
